Z||000003||lou_dias||11-24-2000||09:20 AM||||What generation Firbird do you think it looks like?  Cause if it's the Gen4, then the Firebird looks like the 89 Fiero.  Personally I think the front of the 89GT looks like the new Vette, but the Vette is obviously gotten more curves with age in that nose, and the rear looks like the rear of an NSX...<BR>Almost identical to the rear of an NSX only an NSX's rear is longer because the engine is mounted differently.<P>Wasn't it Nissan that bougth the 89GT moulds, hence the similar silhouette between the Fastback GT's and the 90+ 300ZX...?<P>Somebody wanna make a 300ZX kit for a Fiero?  Add a glass hatch and a new nose with fog lights and gee, what's the new thing for headlight kits on Fiero's...low profile headlights that don't flip and just put a glass cover over the opening...<BR>and remove the black stripe that runs along the length of the car...||||reg||1
Z||000004||82-T/A||11-24-2000||10:23 AM||||In my opinion, the 1989 Fiero GT has got to be the coolest looking car I've ever seen in my life. I would sell a kidney for one of those.. (well, not really). <P>I'm talking about those grey ones.. the pictures that are parked in the grass in front of that building..<P>I heard that car has a 3.4 DOHC V6 with the Getrag... the idea of that motor in that wicked shell... with a 7,500rpm redline... argg.... droool..... whew.. <P>cold shower.. cold shower...<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||11-24-2000||10:26 AM||||The 89 GT prototype is an awsome looking car IMO.  If Pontiac were to put it on sale tomorrow as is, I certainly would eb at the dealer signing on the dotted line!||||reg||1
Z||000006||lou_dias||11-24-2000||10:30 AM||||I'd buy on tomorrow for 22K if it had an updated interior and a hotter 3.4 and an aluminum engine cradle to balance the weight distribution better...<BR>Ok, I'd pay $25k...||||reg||1
